00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:50.440
Question 1 - The Swedish Dude asks Do you
think we’ll be learning more about the other

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.510
important people in Meereen soon?

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.791
Since we saw Hizdahr in episode 6 I think
there’s a really good chance we’ll learn

00:00:55.791 --> 00:00:57.280
more about the other important people around
Meereen.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.789
Daenerys hasn’t gotten any super long scenes
in the last couple of episodes, so she’s

00:01:00.789 --> 00:01:02.800
due for something big soon.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:06.660
Most of the focus right now is around Tyrion’s
Trial, so after that passes I think we’ll

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.890
get at least one long Meereen episode before
the finale.

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:15.170
The show has this weird thing where it likes
to end on really strong Daenerys moments.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:18.030
With the exception of Season 2, which was
that White Walker.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:20.790
That doesn’t guarantee season 4 will end
on a Daenerys moment.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:25.000
But I do think it would be funny if there
was a meta thing going on where each season’s

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.030
end rotated between Fire and Ice.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:30.790
Fire being Daenerys and Ice being stuff going
on up at the Wall.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:37.810
I guess the show has been doing that so far.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:42.200
So technically that would mean this season
would have to end on another scene up in the

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.200
North.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.800
Start your theorycrafting now.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:50.390
Question 2 - Starlight (no avatar) asks what
was Varys motivation to testify against Tyrion

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:52.230
if they were friends?

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:55.980
The interesting thing about Varys is that
he and Tyrion are on the same side.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:58.630
They both want to do what’s best for King’s
Landing.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:02.640
But I think Varys testified against him because
he felt it was more important to his long

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.400
term goals of strengthening the realm.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:09.209
Than the short term goal of rescuing Tyrion.

00:02:09.209 --> 00:02:13.160
Varys is totally willing to throw people under
the bus if it helps keep his plans on course.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:15.950
That’s why he’s just as dangerous as Littlefinger.

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:18.030
Varys just has more noble goals.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.110
He’s not trying to win the throne for himself.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:23.280
I saw a lot of confusion in the comments after
the episode.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:26.480
Because he looked at the throne when he was
talking to Oberyn.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.500
The throne is just a metaphor for his plan.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.890
He doesn’t actually want to be King himself.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:35.540
The really important thing he said was he
never forgets anything.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:38.580
He still cares about Tyrion, it’s just that
testifying was the best course of action at

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:39.580
the time.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.850
Speaking out against Cersei at would have
thrown all his plans into chaos.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:45.870
Question 3 - Adam Thomas asks WTF Shae?

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:50.880
Yeah, this was one of the biggest fist shaking
moments everyone had.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.030
Let’s forget about the books for a second
and just think about what her character has

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.110
been doing on the show.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:03:00.840
I saw two things going on, first she did look
like she was trying to hurt Tyrion.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.220
She was intentionally testifying.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.630
No one was holding a sword to her throat.

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:08.630
But Two, it also looked like Cersei had some
involvement.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:11.960
Shae kept glancing in her direction when she
was testifying.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:17.930
Remember, Cersei’s maid listened to Shae
and Tyrion arguing and we never saw her follow

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:18.930
up with Cersei.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:23.600
So it’s possible that Cersei found out something
was going on and offered Shae money or something

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:24.600
else in return for her testimony.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.320
That being said, I think she still loves Tyrion.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:30.410
She’s just really headstrong and doesn’t
care at all about the other politics going

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.720
on in King’s Landing.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:35.569
Tyrion has been in this really awkward place
politically, all season.

00:03:35.569 --> 00:03:39.020
Having to deal with Sansa and avoid getting
murdered at every moment.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:41.790
He’s been walking on eggshells all season.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.830
And Shae doesn’t care about any of that.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:48.319
I don’t think she fully realizes what’s
going to happen if Tyrion is convicted.

00:03:48.319 --> 00:03:52.250
So if you want to blame her for something,
blame her for ignorance of all the politics

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.880
involved in what’s going on.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:58.050
Question 4 - Cassie Pryor asks Do you think
we’ll see any of the other Greyjoy Uncles

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.640
this season?

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.460
There haven’t been a lot of Greyjoy people
this season.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:07.550
And they didn’t announce any new castings
for them so the chances are pretty slim.

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:11.510
The Moat Cailin Ramsay Snow plot deals with
the Ironborn, so it’s possible they could

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:12.510
be involved.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:14.209
But the producers and HBO haven’t made any
announcements.

00:04:14.209 --> 00:04:15.599
So it’s unlikely.

00:04:15.599 --> 00:04:20.110
If you’re not familiar with all the Greyjoys,
there are a lot of secondary characters that

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:21.110
get mentioned.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:30.240
But the show has a habit of cutting characters
out and giving their lines to other characters.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.930
Like with the Brave Companions or Strong Belwas.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:36.630
Question 5 - Lenny asks When will they start
casting Season 5?

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:39.640
Usually we start to hear casting news during
the summer.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:43.030
So plan to hear a few things around Comic
Con in July.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:45.270
They don’t cast everyone at once either.

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:47.950
So they’ll be announcing new people all
the way into the fall.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:51.370
They have started scouting locations, which
is one of the first things they do before

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:53.650
they cast people and start preparing new episodes.

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:54.650
First they have to find out where things are
going to be filmed.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:05:01.880
A lot of you have been asking me about Dorne,
I can’t confirm we’ll see Dorne next year.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:06.300
But when they announce the new shooting locations
we’ll get a pretty good idea.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:07.710
Usually those don’t stay secret.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:12.470
So if they end up filming near a desert we’ll
have our answer.

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:17.240
Question 6 - BDDestro asks What would happen
if Daenerys always let her dragons roam free

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:18.880
and didn’t keep them caged up?

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.000
And are they evil or just playful?

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:29.000
Based on the literature inside the show, Dragons
will just keep growing if they have enough

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.460
food and space.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:33.430
If you confine them, they won’t grow as
much.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:38.250
So if Daenerys just let them roam free and
live out in the open, potentially they’d

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.270
get as big as Balerion the Black Dread.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.419
Here’s a picture for scale.

00:05:42.419 --> 00:05:45.940
The problem with that is that they’d need
a massive food supply, so they’d have to

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.490
eat everything in sight.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:52.449
And they are playful but because they’re
deadly wild animals, when they do play, they

00:05:52.449 --> 00:05:54.110
can tear things to shreds.

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:55.210
Or incinerate them.

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:58.810
There’s always stories about people raising
wild animals like tigers or alligators and

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:01.140
then having to give them to nature preserves
when they get too big.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:03.449
Because no matter how much you train them,
at some point their primal instinct will kick

00:06:03.449 --> 00:06:06.139
in and they could kill a bunch of people.

00:06:06.139 --> 00:06:11.380
Question 7 - Andrew Jones asks Why would Theon
think Yara showing up was a trick?

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:15.900
That’s just how brainwashed he is.

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:20.949
We saw a lot of the torture during season
3, but Ramsay is still psychologically abusing

00:06:20.949 --> 00:06:21.949
him.

00:06:21.949 --> 00:06:23.800
So the Reek persona has taken over.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:28.520
It’s not a split personality like Golum
on Lord of The Rings, there aren’t two separate

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:29.880
identities living inside him.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:34.630
He’s just completely this Reek person that
lives as an appendage of Ramsay now.

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:38.380
He probably didn’t even realize who Yara
was, all he saw was someone coming to kidnap

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:39.380
him.

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:45.690
Question 8 - Jaime Quirkle asks How could
Jaime become lord of Casterly Rock so quickly?

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:51.430
You’re asking about the practical aspects
of going from the Kingsguard to being a regular

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:52.509
Lord again.

00:06:52.509 --> 00:06:56.610
Normally taking the oath of the Kingsguard
is a lifelong thing, just like taking the

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:57.610
Black.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:07:01.800
But because Tywin Lannister is the Hand of
the King and the most powerful man in Westeros,

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:02.800
he does whatever he wants.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:06.000
So they’re just sweeping a lot of the traditional
rules under the Rug.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:10.180
I also saw a lot of you ask me for my opinion
on whether or not Jaime would have gone through

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:11.180
with it.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:14.180
And yes, if Tyrion had not messed with the
plan by demanding trial by combat, Jaime would

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:15.740
have gone back to Casterly Rock.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:20.370
He still loves Cersei deep down, but it seems
like their sexual relationship is over.

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:24.740
Question 9 - Misti asks Does the Crown know
where the Mountain is right now?

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:27.590
Yes, Tywin Lannister sent him to the Riverlands
in Season 2 to just wreak havoc and cause

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:30.800
problems for Robb Stark’s allies, mostly
the Tullys.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:34.990
He was at Harrenhaal when Arya, Hot Pie and
Jaquen H’gar were there.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:38.430
But he kind of went rogue and started going
crazy all over the locals.

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:41.419
So Tywin hasn’t really been doing anything
with him lately.

00:07:41.419 --> 00:07:42.570
But he does know where he is.

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:46.440
And the Mountain is still one of his bannermen,
so he’ll do anything Tywin tells him to

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:47.440
do.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:49.660
It’s just that the Mountain is one of the
most evil people on the show.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:54.750
I think the only reason Tywin Lannister uses
him is because he’s so effective as a weapon.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:59.160
Question 10 - Robynskie asks how did Pycelle
get Sansa’s Necklace?

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:02.229
Whenever Littlefinger killed him and dumped
him in the boat he dropped the necklace in

00:08:02.229 --> 00:08:03.229
with him.

00:08:03.229 --> 00:08:05.330
And they were in the bay right near the castle.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:07.410
So he would have drifted to shore eventually.

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:11.800
So Littlefinger meant for the authorities
to find the body, and as the Maester, it would

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:13.880
have fallen to Pycelle to examine the body.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:14.880
Where he would have found the necklace.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:19.940
and one last Bonus Question - Claudio asks
Do you know when the other books will be published?

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:24.310
So right now the only book that’s been officially
announced is the World of Ice and Fire.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:29.100
It’s a lot of the information from the Wiki
and maps put together with a lot of cool artwork.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:30.319
It’s not a novel.

00:08:30.319 --> 00:08:33.200
That’s being released October 28th.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:37.479
Winds of Winter hasn’t been announced, but
there’s been so many new excerpts released

00:08:37.479 --> 00:08:41.490
this year it’s possible we could see that
book before the Season 5 premiere of the show.

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:44.980
I’m expecting that around the same time
Season 4 premiered.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:49.180
So fingers crossed we get the book by Spring
2015.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:50.959
Maybe even Christmas this year.

00:08:50.959 --> 00:08:56.140
Don’t be surprised if they announce a release
date at Comic Con.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:57.470
The final Song of Ice and Fire Book.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:58.470
Dream of Spring?

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:06.380
No idea on that one, just take the amount
of time Winds of Winter took and use that

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.380
as an estimate.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:10.010
So like 2018-2019.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:14.890
So I think the show will probably pass the
books in Season 7.

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:17.170
Assuming they get 8 seasons total.

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:18.850
Thanks so much everyone for submitting questions.

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:21.750
I always love being able to answer your questions
directly.

